## 1. DEFINITION

PRSL-AI Intelligent Storage Lifecycle is the infrastructure intelligence layer responsible for managing the physical lifecycle, placement, prioritization, retention, optimization, migration, expiration and removal of data across iRiel Devices and authorized storage resources.

It exists to ensure that storage is not treated as passive capacity, but as an intelligent and governed resource within the Personal Intelligence Environment.

---

## 2. CORE PRINCIPLE

The canonical principle is:

> Intelligent Storage Lifecycle manages how information occupies physical storage without independently determining the semantic value of that information.

Storage must adapt to the needs of the Personal Intelligence Environment.

The user should not be required to manually manage every aspect of storage created by continuous intelligence, context, memory and local computation.

---

## 3. PRIMARY PURPOSE

The Intelligent Storage Lifecycle exists to:

- Optimize storage utilization.
- Preserve required local data.
- Reduce unnecessary retention.
- Manage temporary data.
- Manage caches.
- Support local intelligence.
- Support offline operation.
- Enable intelligent data placement.
- Support cross-device continuity.
- Reduce unnecessary duplication.
- Protect available storage capacity.
- Support privacy through controlled retention.
- Maintain predictable device performance.

---

## 4. WHAT IT IS NOT

Intelligent Storage Lifecycle is not:

- A file manager.
- A personal memory system.
- A privacy policy engine.
- A security system.
- A replacement for iRiel Memory.
- A replacement for iRiel Context.
- A replacement for Governance.
- An automatic deletion engine.
- A cloud-storage requirement.
- A mechanism for deciding the semantic value of personal information.

