## 6. RESPONSIBILITY SEPARATION

The architecture maintains a strict separation of responsibilities.

iRiel Context
→ Determines what is relevant now.

iRiel Memory
→ Determines what should remain available for continuity.

Memory Manager
→ Manages the lifecycle of logical memory.

Memory Placement
→ Determines appropriate storage location.

Governance
→ Determines what policies and permissions apply.

Intelligent Storage Lifecycle
→ Manages the physical lifecycle of stored data.

iRiel Devices
→ Provide computation and physical storage resources.

